# Docker build context for the backend image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file the build context includes
# `.env` (real secrets) and `dev.log`. Neither belongs in an image layer.

# Secrets — the container is configured by environment at run time, never by a
# baked-in file. `.env.example` is excluded too; the build does not need it.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Logs and local artifacts
*.log
logs/
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Dependencies are installed in-image by `npm ci`
node_modules/

# Build output is produced in-image by `npm run build`
dist/

# VCS / editor / OS noise
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Test caches
.cache/
*.tsbuildinfo
